_PccuEntry('Difficult airway escalation', 'Respiratory Support', <_PccuSection>[_PccuSection('Clinical overview', <String>['Declare difficulty early, limit repeated attempts and prioritize oxygenation over tracheal intubation.']), _PccuSection('Initial stabilization', <String>['Call anesthesia/ENT/PCCU and bring the difficult-airway cart.','Use the most experienced operator, optimize position and move deliberately through Plan A/B/C/D.']), _PccuSection('Disease-specific treatment / settings', <String>['Consider video laryngoscopy, bougie/stylet and supraglottic airway.','In cannot-intubate/cannot-oxygenate physiology, proceed to the institution’s emergency front-of-neck access pathway.']), _PccuSection('Monitoring', <String>['Time, attempts, saturation nadir, ventilation between attempts and hemodynamics.']), _PccuSection('Expected response', <String>['Oxygenation maintained and airway secured with the least traumatic method.']), _PccuSection('Failure criteria and escalation', <String>['Two failed attempts by experienced operators, inability to mask ventilate or falling saturation despite rescue maneuvers.']), _PccuSection('Complications / cautions', <String>['Airway trauma, edema, hypoxic arrest and task fixation.']), _PccuSection('Sources and local verification', <String>['Difficult Airway Society pediatric algorithm; local difficult-airway plan.'])], 'DIFFICULT AIRWAY ESCALATION\\n- ABCDE stabilization and confirm current measured weight.\\n- Apply the disease-specific Difficult airway escalation pathway and local formulary/equipment standards.\\n- Define objective monitoring targets and a reassessment interval.\\n- Escalate to senior/PCCU support for failure criteria or deterioration.\\n- Verify all doses, concentrations and settings independently.'),
