_PccuEntry('Severe asthma', 'Disease-Specific Respiratory Pathways', <_PccuSection>[_PccuSection('Clinical overview', <String>['Severe exacerbation is suggested by marked work of breathing, inability to speak/feed, hypoxemia, poor air entry or exhaustion. A quiet chest is ominous.']), _PccuSection('Initial stabilization', <String>['Give oxygen to target saturation, repeated/continuous inhaled salbutamol and ipratropium, and systemic corticosteroid early.','Obtain IV access and senior/PCCU review when response is incomplete.']), _PccuSection('Disease-specific treatment / settings', <String>['IV magnesium sulfate is a common early adjunct in severe disease.','Continuous salbutamol, IV beta-agonist or aminophylline require monitored specialist use. Ketamine may support induction or refractory bronchospasm but is not routine first-line therapy.']), _PccuSection('Monitoring', <String>['Clinical asthma score, HR, RR, air entry, speech, SpO₂, potassium, lactate and gas when fatigue or deterioration is suspected.']), _PccuSection('Expected response', <String>['Improved air entry, reduced work of breathing and ability to space bronchodilator therapy.']), _PccuSection('Failure criteria and escalation', <String>['Rising CO₂, exhaustion, altered mental status, worsening hypoxemia, bradycardia or absent air entry.']), _PccuSection('Complications / cautions', <String>['Hypokalemia, lactic acidosis, tachyarrhythmia, dynamic hyperinflation, pneumothorax and peri-intubation arrest.']), _PccuSection('Sources and local verification', <String>['GINA 2025; Children’s Hospital Colorado asthma pathway; local severe-asthma protocol.'])], 'SEVERE ASTHMA\\n- ABCDE stabilization and confirm current measured weight.\\n- Apply the disease-specific Severe asthma pathway and local formulary/equipment standards.\\n- Define objective monitoring targets and a reassessment interval.\\n- Escalate to senior/PCCU support for failure criteria or deterioration.\\n- Verify all doses, concentrations and set